{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "2SA",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now it came to pass after the death of Saul, when David had returned from the slaughter of the Amalekites, and David had abode two days in Ziklag;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It came even to pass on the third day, that behold, a man came out of the camp from Saul with his clothes rent, and earth upon his head: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it was, when he came to David, that he fell to the earth, and did obeisance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David said to him, From whence comest thou? And he said to him, Out of the camp of Israel have I escaped.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David said to him, How went the matter? I pray thee, tell me. And he answered, That the people have fled from the battle, and many of the people also have fallen, and are dead; and Saul and Jonathan his son are dead also.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David said to the young man that told him, How knowest thou that Saul and Jonathan his son are dead?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the young man that told him said, As I happened by chance upon mount Gilboa, behold, Saul leaned upon his spear; and lo, the chariots and horsemen followed hard after him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he looked behind him, he saw me, and called to me. And I answered, Here ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to me, Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou? And I answered him, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an Amalekite.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He said to me again, Stand, I pray thee, upon me, and slay me: for anguish is come upon me, because my life ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yet whole in me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So I stood upon him, and slew him, because I was sure that he could not live after that he had fallen: and I took the crown that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon his head, and the bracelet that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on his arm, and have brought them hither to my lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then David took hold on his clothes, and rent them; and likewise all the men that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they mourned and wept, and fasted until evening, for Saul and for Jonathan his son, and for the people of the LORD, and for the house of Israel; because they had fallen by the sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David said to the young man that told him, Whence ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou? And he answered, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the son of a stranger, an Amalekite.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David said to him, How wast thou not afraid to stretch forth thy hand to destroy the LORD'S anointed?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David called one of the young men, and said, Go near, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fall upon him. And he smote him that he died.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David said to him, Thy blood ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon thy head; for thy mouth hath testified against thee, saying, I have slain the LORD'S anointed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David lamented with this lamentation over Saul, and over Jonathan his son:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(Also he bade them teach the children of Judah ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the use of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the bow: behold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " written in the book of Jasher.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The beauty of Israel is slain upon thy high places: how are the mighty fallen!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Tell ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not in Gath, publish ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not in the streets of Askelon; lest the daughters of the Philistines rejoice, lest the daughters of the uncircumcised triumph.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye mountains of Gilboa, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "let there be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no dew, neither rain upon you, nor fields of offerings: for there the shield of the mighty is vilely cast away, the shield of Saul, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as though he had",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "been",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " anointed with oil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From the blood of the slain, from the fat of the mighty, the bow of Jonathan turned not back, and the sword of Saul returned not empty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Saul and Jonathan ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lovely and pleasant in their lives, and in their death they were not divided: they were swifter than eagles, they were stronger than lions.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye daughters of Israel, weep over Saul, who clothed you in scarlet, with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "other",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " delights, who put ornaments of gold upon your apparel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How are the mighty fallen in the midst of the battle! O Jonathan ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thou wast",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " slain in thy high places.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am distressed for thee, my brother Jonathan: very pleasant hast thou been to me: thy love to me was wonderful, passing the love of women.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.1.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.1.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How have the mighty fallen, and the weapons of war perished!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
